.TH CWE-347 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-347 \- Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not verify, or incorrectly verifies, the cryptographic signature for data.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB6\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2020\-1464
Microsoft Windows, added 2021\-11\-03.
.PP
Microsoft Windows Spoofing Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Microsoft Windows contains a spoofing vulnerability when Windows incorrectly validates file signatures, allowing an attacker to bypass security features and load improperly signed files.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-05\-03.
.PP
